  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Quick finishes – small-sided game with wall players",
  "description": "A 3v3 small-sided game with goalies in one zone, about 15 × 10 metres (smaller for younger players). Two or three other teams stand at six points around the area as wall players (marked J): they always pass the puck straight back to the team that played it to them, so the puck is almost always in play. If the puck still goes out, the goalie on that side plays a new puck out to their team.\n\nThe aim is to find quick shots in the space that opens up, and to read the situation – smart, accurate shots matter more than hard ones. Swap the playing teams and the wall players on the fly every 1.5 minutes, for example over 2 × 12 minutes. Limit the wall players' touches to suit the level: three, two or one. The diagram is not to scale and the goalies are not drawn.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Use the wall to get past a defender: pass and skate straight into the space."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Shoot on your first or second touch as soon as a chance opens."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Accuracy before power – aim for the corners and use where the goalie stands."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Wall players: pass in front of the skater so they can shoot first time."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 3,
